    "blocks": [
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Assertions work the same way as any AssertJ assertions. The support provides dedicated assert objects for the various pieces of the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MvcTestResult"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", as shown in the following example:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./HotelControllerTests[tag=get,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If a request fails, the exchange does not throw the exception. Rather, you can assert that the result of the exchange has failed:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./HotelControllerTests[tag=failure,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The request could also fail unexpectedly, that is the exception thrown by the handler has not been handled and is thrown as is. You can still use "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ".hasFailed()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": ".failure()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " but any attempt to access part of the result will throw an exception as the exchange hasn’t completed."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The AssertJ support for "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "MvcTestResult"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " provides JSON support via "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "bodyJson()"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JSONPath"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://github.com/jayway/JsonPath"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is available, you can apply an expression on the JSON document. The returned value provides convenient methods to return a dedicated assert object for the various supported JSON data types:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./FamilyControllerTests[tag=extract-asmap,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can also convert the raw content to any of your data types as long as the message converter is configured properly:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./FamilyControllerTests[tag=extract-convert,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Converting to a target "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Class"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " provides a generic assert object. For more complex types, you may want to use "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "AssertFactory"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " instead that returns a dedicated assert type, if possible:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./FamilyControllerTests[tag=extract-convert-assert-factory,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "JSONAssert"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://jsonassert.skyscreamer.org"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " is also supported. The body of the response can be matched against a "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "Resource"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or a content. If the content ends with `.json ` we look for a file matching that name on the classpath:"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "include-code::./FamilyControllerTests[tag=assert-file,indent=0]"
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "If you prefer to use another library, you can provide an implementation of "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "id": null,
                    "inlines": [
                      {
                        "kind": "text",
                        "value": "JsonComparator"
                      }
                    ],
                    "kind": "monospace",
                    "roles": []
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "link",
                "target": "https://docs.spring.io/spring-framework/docs/6.2.0/javadoc-api/org/springframework/test/json/JsonComparator.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
